%%{init: {'sequence': {'mirrorActors': false}}}%%
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant FE as Frontend
    participant API as Order API
    participant ODB as Order DB
    participant OUT as Outbox
    participant K as Kafka
    participant EX as Execution Consumer
    participant Q as Market Data API
    participant ID as Idempotency Ledger
    participant TDB as Trade / Holdings / Cash DB
    participant N as Portfolio / Notification Consumer
    participant DLQ as Dead Letter Topic

    U->>FE: Submit order
    FE->>API: POST /orders
    API->>ODB: validate + persist Order(PENDING)
    API->>OUT: store OrderAccepted event
    API-->>FE: 202 Accepted + orderId

    OUT->>K: publish OrderAccepted{eventId, orderId, userId, ticker, side, qty, limitPrice}
    Note over K,EX: Kafka can redeliver the same message more than once.
    K-->>EX: OrderAccepted
    EX->>ID: check eventId / orderId

    alt already processed
        ID-->>EX: duplicate
        EX-->>K: ack without side effects
    else first delivery
        ID-->>EX: not processed
        EX->>Q: fetch current quote

        alt quote unavailable or retry limit hit
            EX->>DLQ: park message after retries
            EX-->>K: nack / retry
        else quote available
            EX->>TDB: begin transaction
            EX->>TDB: write Trade
            EX->>TDB: update Holding
            EX->>TDB: update CashHolding
            EX->>TDB: update Order status = EXECUTED
            EX->>ID: mark eventId processed
            EX-->>K: commit offset / ack
            EX->>K: publish OrderExecuted{orderId, tradeId, executionPrice}
            K-->>N: OrderExecuted
        end
    end

   